      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Minimizing logistical risk in Zone B is a valid concern, but solely prioritizing predictable areas like Zone A misses the broader goal of regional recovery. While Zone A has a stronger tax base, its concentrated wealth may not support the productive sectors that stabilize the entire area. Focusing on Zone D addresses populations whose immediate stability is critical to maintaining the necessary labor supply for large-scale reconstruction across all zones.",
      "source": "target",
